# {{blueprintName}}, a JGen blueprint

A [JGen](https://jgen.chenile.org) blueprint. Everything it generates lives in
`src/main/resources/{{blueprintName}}-template/`; its inputs are declared in
`src/main/resources/META-INF/blueprint.json`, and optional Java hooks are in
`src/main/java/org/chenile/jgen/blueprint/{{blueprintName}}/`.

## Use it

{{#githubRepository}}
```bash
jgen -g github:{{githubRepository}} -o input.json     # emit a sample input
jgen -f input.json                                    # generate
```
{{/githubRepository}}
{{^githubRepository}}
```bash
jgen -g github:<owner>/<repo> -o input.json     # emit a sample input
jgen -f input.json                              # generate
```
{{/githubRepository}}

Or, without publishing: `mvn package`, copy `target/bp-{{blueprintName}}-*.jar` to `~/.jgen/blueprints/`, and run
`jgen -g {{blueprintName}} -o input.json`.

## Develop it

```bash
mvn test        # loads the blueprint like JGen does and generates the starter project
mvn package     # builds target/bp-{{blueprintName}}-<version>.jar
```

- `__projectName__` in a path becomes an input value; files ending in `.mustache` are rendered with the inputs;
  folders named `%%input=value%%` are kept only when the input matches. See the
  [template reference](https://jgen.chenile.org/template-conventions/).
- Add inputs in `blueprint.json`, with validation rules such as `JAVA_IDENTIFIER` or `HTTP_URL`
  ([input validation](https://jgen.chenile.org/input-validation/)).
- Add Java only for what templates cannot express, in the init hook
  ([write your own blueprint](https://jgen.chenile.org/authoring/)).
- Keep `jgen-base` at `provided` scope; shade any other library your hooks need.

## Release it

Push a version tag. `.github/workflows/release.yml` builds the jar with that version and attaches it to a GitHub
release:

```bash
git tag 0.2.0 && git push origin 0.2.0
```

Add the topic `jgen-blueprint` to the repository so people can find it.
